commit fa4ef88a2b93233885270410687a94f84f484f48
Author: wynn5a <winminy@163.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 10:50:23 2026 +0800

    local_inference: speak the OpenAI Responses protocol

    Add Schema::OpenaiResponses: a stateless (store: false) request with the
    system prompt in instructions, function_call / function_call_output items
    paired by call_id, and a stream parser that derives the stop reason from
    the response status and output items. Reasoning is not replayed.

    A custom endpoint set to "OpenAI Responses" now speaks it; before, it was
    silently sent Chat Completions. An error reported inside a stream ends it
    with Error::ProviderStream, and rate-limit codes map to QuotaLimit.

    This is steps 1-3 of specs/plans/openai-responses.md, the groundwork for
    Sign in with ChatGPT. Built-in OpenAI keys stay on Chat Completions until
    this has settled.

